  "summary": {
    "en": "Gangs attacked inmates in two Ecuadorian prisons, killing eight and wounding ten, and the government transferred opposition leader Luisa González to Riobamba Prison and placed her in preventive detention on alleged money-laundering charges. President Noboa has intensified militarization and political repression as Ecuador aligns with external security interests. The crisis previously noted two battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.",
